{"archetypes":[{"name":"generator-contract","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan asserts codex-implementer.md and cursor-implementer.md are regenerated by named generator scripts with specific sed substitutions, and that make test-check-generators enforces this — none of these claims are verified against actual repo state.","prompt_body":"The plan states that `agents/codex-implementer.md` and `agents/cursor-implementer.md` will be regenerated by `bash scripts/generate-codex-implementer.sh` and `bash scripts/generate-cursor-implementer.sh`, with no hand edits, and that `make test-check-generators` enforces regeneration parity. Verify that both generator scripts exist in the repo and open them to check whether they perform the sed substitutions the plan describes (TOOL_COMMIT_STDERR, NEVER #2 wording). Verify that `test-check-generators` is a real Makefile target and inspect what it actually checks. If any generator script is missing, does not apply the described substitutions, or the Makefile target is absent, the plan's 'no hand edits' guarantee is unverifiable and maintainers will silently diverge the generated files. Also confirm that `test-codex-implementer.sh` and `test-cursor-implementer.sh` are integrated into `make test-codex-implementer` and `make test-cursor-implementer` targets as the plan assumes. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"line-anchor-verification","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan names five specific emit_bailed call sites in step2-implement.sh at lines 486, 490, 507, 534, and 548 that must be consolidated; wrong line numbers mean the implementer targets the wrong code and misses real call sites.","prompt_body":"Open `skills/implement/scripts/step2-implement.sh` and verify that `emit_bailed \"manifest-schema-invalid\"` (or equivalent) actually appears at or near lines 486, 490, 507, 534, and 548 as the plan claims. Count all occurrences of `manifest-schema-invalid` in the file to determine whether the plan's list is complete — any call site not covered by the consolidating function will silently retain the old bail-without-recovery behavior and make Tests M1/M4 pass locally while leaving real production escapes. Also verify that the existing `emit_kv ORCHESTRATOR_EDIT_AUTHORITY forbidden` emit sites cited by the plan (lines 262, 841, 850, 867) are real — the pair-invariant argument depends on these being the only non-recovery places that emit ORCHESTRATOR_EDIT_AUTHORITY, and a missed site could allow a double-emit that breaks the grep -c == 1 invariant the plan claims Test M5 will pin. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"sync-surface-adequacy","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan duplicates the full manifest schema into the implementer base prompt, relying on a string-presence grep and an Edit-in-sync prose note to prevent the duplicate from drifting — this is the exact class of documentation-pointer degradation the issue report identifies as root cause.","prompt_body":"The plan creates a dual-maintenance schema surface: the canonical schema in `skills/implement/references/codex-manifest-schema.md` and an inline template copy in `agents/_implementer-base.md`, held in sync by an 'Edit-in-sync note' in the schema reference and a `grep -F -q '\"schema_version\": \"1\"'` presence test in each implementer test script. Open `codex-manifest-schema.md` and compare its complete required-field list against the jq self-validation block proposed in the plan — verify that every field the dispatcher validates in `step2-implement.sh` (including `files_touched`, `summary_bullets`, `tests_added_or_modified`, `todos_left`, `oos_observations`) is also validated by the proposed jq -e block, with no field silently omitted. Check whether a grep for `\"schema_version\": \"1\"` is sufficient to catch a drifted template that has the right schema_version but wrong field names (e.g., `summary` instead of `summary_bullets`); if not, the regression guard the plan adds to the implementer tests would pass on a broken template. Also check whether `agent-lint.toml` or any existing linter already enforces structural constraints on agent prompt files that could supplement or replace the string-presence check. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
